{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Three evaluate() paths in the MCP<->library parity gate ship untested. Raised as non-blocking\nadvisories by the LLM code review on Gerrit 2503 and deferred there; filed here rather than dropped.\n\n## Scope\n\nAdd pure-function regression coverage against the already-injectable\n`evaluate(live, manifest)` behavior in `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py`.\nNo production behavior change is intended.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A test proves a declared divergence whose MCP and library surfaces have\n  since converged is reported as a stale divergence failure by\n  `_check_divergences` through `evaluate(live, manifest)`.\n- [ ] A test proves `merge_declarations`/`--update` carry existing divergence\n  reasons forward and write an empty-reason stub for a newly-diverging tool, so\n  a real divergence cannot be silently laundered.\n- [ ] Tests prove `_check_normalization` detects both `schema_version` changes\n  and `normalization.library_only_params` changes between live data and the\n  manifest.\n\n## Testing\n\nRun `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_library_parity.py`\nand the pre-push `make verify` gate from the ticket worktree."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788747658213791001,"uuid":"c00ce324-ba91-403b-93fe-42acf7506bf4"}